.TH "DOTBEE" "1" "August 24, 2026" "dotbee 0.9.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
dotbee \- Easy to use dotfiles manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]dotbee\f[R] OPTIONS
.SH DESCRIPTION
dotbee is a lightweight manager designed to simplify the handling of
dotfiles across different environments.
It allows users to fetch configurations, manage symlinks, and
synchronize profiles with ease.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-c, \-\-config\f[R] FILE
Specify a custom path to the dotbee configuration file.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Do not perform any actions; only print the operations that would be
executed.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Print help information.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the version number of dotbee.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
completion, c
Generate shell completions for the specified shell.
.RS
Supported shells: bash, zsh, fish, elvish.
.RE
.TP
doctor, dr
Perform a system check to show currently used configs and the status of
active symlinks.
.TP
init, i
Initialize dotbee in the current environment.
.TP
list, ls
List all available configurations currently managed by dotbee.
.TP
purge, p
Remove and purge existing symlinks managed by dotbee.
.TP
sync, s OPTIONS
Synchronize configurations.
.RS
\(enprofile PROFILE Specify the target profile to sync.
.RE
.TP
fetch, f URL
Download a dotfiles repository from the specified Git URL.
.TP
edit, e
Open the dotbee.toml configuration file in the default system editor.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize dotbee for the first time:
.IP
.EX
dotbee init
.EE
.PP
Fetch a remote dotfiles repository:
.IP
.EX
dotbee fetch https://github.com/rogue\-sly/dotfiles.git
.EE
.PP
Sync a specific profile without making actual changes:
.IP
.EX
dotbee \-\-dry\-run sync \-\-profile work
.EE
.PP
Generate completions for Zsh:
.IP
.EX
dotbee completion zsh > \(ti/.zsh/_dotbee
.EE
.SH FILES
\(ti/.config/dotbee/config.toml
.IP
.EX
Configuration file for dotbee
.EE
.PP
\(ti/.local/state/dotbee/dotbee.lock
.IP
.EX
Prevent multiple concurrent processes
.EE
.PP
\(ti/.local/state/dotbee/state.json
.IP
.EX
Ensure symlink integrity
.EE
.PP
\(ti/.local/share/dotbee/
.IP
.EX
Location where dotfiles repository files are stored
.EE
